  {
   "comment": "_Disclosure: I work at viaSocket._\n\nIf you're considering external task provider integrations, viaSocket Embed might help. It's a hosted widget that gives your users access to 2,300+ app integrations (Gmail, Slack, HubSpot, Google Sheets, and many task/project tools) directly in your UI. Users connect their accounts and build automations between apps without leaving fluid-calendar. We could submit an optional, off-by-default PR (env-gated, one backend route to sign tokens, one UI entry point, docs) so maintainers control whether to enable it. Would you be open to that approach for this feature?",
